fix: the shipped injection budget could not hold a normal workspace

The default was 16000 bytes. In a mature workspace that is not enough for
PROJECT.md plus DECISIONS.md plus the default number of session entries -- this
workspace needs 26289 -- so every session carried the 未注入 omission footer and
the model was permanently reasoning from a partial picture. The default is now 64000.

- lib/index.js: the default in the Config schema and in normalizeConfig, plus a
  comment at the declaration saying what the key actually is -- a ceiling the
  assembler stops degrading at, not a size it fills to. The block is only ever as
  big as PROJECT.md + DECISIONS.md + sessionEntriesInjected entries; SESSIONS.md in
  full is never injected however large the budget is.
- README/DESIGN: the config table said "注入总字节预算", which reads like a quota. It
  now says what the key is, and which knob actually controls how much log gets in.
- A new check pins the guarantee rather than the number: a workspace with ~37 KB of
  memory must inject without an omission note under the shipped defaults. Verified
  that it fails with the old 16000 and passes with 64000.

The over-budget check still drives its own 2000-byte budget, so it never depended
on the default.

Suites: 60 host + 6 render + 27 interaction.
